MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzE2NDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20316467?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula","html_url":"https://github.com/badsectoracula","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-27T19:16:27Z","updated_at":"2024-11-27T19:16:27Z","body":"I tried this PR, seems to work as advertised.\r\n\r\nTwo comments though:\r\n\r\n1. Why do you cast the selection to `Node` and check for `nullptr` in line 5428 `Node *sp = Object::cast_to<Node>(selection.front()->get());`? The object you get is already a `Node` and there should not be null objects in the selection. I removed the cast in my copy of this PR,  checked the behavior and didn't notice anything weird with trying to make cameras, was there something you found?\r\n2. PRs should be single commits to keep history clean but you have 3 commits in yours. I think it *should* be simple to fix with an interactive git rebase and mark all later commits to be squished. Check the docs for how to do that: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/workflow/pr_workflow.html#the-interactive-rebase\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2504621839/reactions","tot